charseg DEFAULT model — provenance, licensing, and measured quality
===================================================================
Artifact:  sentence/charseg/data/charseg_model_clean.tsv  (hashed averaged-
           perceptron char-level Thai sentence-boundary classifier)
Loader:    sentence/charseg/default.go  -> charseg.Default()  (and charseg.Split)
Built:     2026-07-06

WHY THIS MODEL EXISTS
---------------------
It is the recommended, license-clean default for general Thai text. It is
trained FROM SCRATCH on permissive / own / public-domain data ONLY — no CRF
teacher, no distillation, no ORCHID/TED/LST20, no ShareAlike text — so the
shipped weights are safe to release and relicense (MIT/CC0) and give back to the
community. The comparison baseline in the tables below, the word-level CRF
sentence/crf.Default (crfcut), is shown for reference only; its published model
label is CC-BY-4.0 but it was trained on ORCHID (CC-BY-NC-SA), TED
(CC-BY-NC-ND) and other ShareAlike corpora, so it is marked "(taint)" and was
NOT used to train, distill, or label this model.

The char-level architecture, feature hashing, averaged-perceptron trainer and
candidate definition (sentence/charseg/*.go) are our own original code. Only the
*weights* here are trained on clean data.

TRAINING DATA — every source is own / CC0 / PD / MIT / CC-BY (NO NC/ND/SA)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Tatoeba Thai sentences — PRIMARY "where to cut" signal.
   License: CC BY 2.0 FR (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/fr/).
   Source : https://downloads.tatoeba.org/exports/per_language/tha/ (snapshot
            2026-07-06, 6,848 rows; 2 non-Thai rows dropped -> 6,846 clean).
   Use    : 500 sentences held out as a released gold TEST set (see manifest);
            the remaining 6,348 are concatenated with single spaces into 24,000
            synthetic multi-sentence documents. Because each Tatoeba entry is
            exactly one sentence, every join is an EXACT (100%-correct) sentence
            boundary and every intra-sentence space is an exact non-boundary.
            Attribution: "Contains sentences from the Tatoeba Project, CC BY 2.0 FR."
   NOTE   : Concatenation joins with SPACES (not run-together no-space joins),
            because this char-level engine can only cut at orthographic
            candidate positions (whitespace / terminal punct / opening quote),
            and every standard benchmark also concatenates sentences with spaces.

2. Wisesight social-media text — realistic message boundaries.
   License: CC0-1.0.  Provided as data/incoming/cc0_gov_social.jsonl.
   Use    : exact message/sentence boundaries; supplies realistic social-chat
            phrasing and the low-boundary-rate intra-message space negatives.
   Weight : 0.15 (subsampled — full weight over-suppresses recall).

3. thaigov-v2 government-news corpus — formal-register negatives.
   License: Public Domain (dataset declared PD by PyThaiNLP; Thai Official
            Information Act B.E. 2540; repo code Apache-2.0).
   Source : https://github.com/PyThaiNLP/thaigov-v2-corpus
   Use    : SHORT lines (<=90 runes) only, each a single high-precision
            paragraph/headline unit with its end as the boundary. Short lines
            minimise the "under-split" mislabeling that long paragraphs cause.
            The sibling-provided FULL-document thaigov records (paragraph-level
            cuts, ~6% of spaces are boundaries) were EXCLUDED from training
            (weight 0) precisely to avoid teaching under-segmentation.
   Weight : 0.20.

4. TLC (Thai Literature Corpus, MIT) + Wikisource (Public Domain) — literary/
   formal register. License: MIT (tlc) / PD (wikisource). Structure-derived
   (paragraph/verse) cuts; under-split like thaigov full-docs, so weight 0.04.
   Improves academic/formal-news and UD scores. Provided as
   data/incoming/literature.jsonl.

5. Own novel-platform text (thai-novel.com) — dialogue/quote silver.
   License: OWN PLATFORM (used with permission; our data).
   Use    : char-level orthographic silver (closing quote / terminal punct /
            before opening quote). Weight 0.05 (low — its silver is negative-
            heavy; higher weights depress recall).

NOT USED IN TRAINING (test-only or excluded):
   crf.Default/crfcut (teacher taint), ORCHID, TED, LST20, FLORES, Thai-
   Wikipedia (SA), UD_Thai-PUD, UD_Thai-TUD-test, and the 6 hand-crafted gold
   sets — all reserved for EVALUATION ONLY.

FINAL TRAINING MIX (after dedup + per-source weighting)
-------------------------------------------------------
  source            pool docs   weight
  tatoeba-concat       24,000    1.00
  thaigov-v2 (short)    1,183    0.20
  wisesight (CC0)       2,670    0.15
  tlc (MIT)                60    0.04
  wikisource (PD)          18    0.04
  own-novel (OWN)       2,721    0.05
  (sibling full-doc thaigov: 10,000 docs -> weight 0.00, excluded: under-split)
  Dedup removed: 208 exact + 4 near-duplicate docs.
  Effective training set: 23,493 documents, 4,187,279 runes, 118,356 boundaries.
  Trainer: averaged perceptron, 20-bit hashed weights, 12 iterations, seed 42.

NO TEST LEAKAGE (proof: leak check over all training sources)
-------------------------------------------------------------
  1,490 eval gold sentences (>=10 chars, whitespace-normalised) checked against
  every training source:
    - Tatoeba raw:            0 exact overlaps
    - own-novel:              0 exact; 1 incidental short-phrase substring
    - cc0_gov_social:         0 exact; 2 incidental short-phrase substrings
  The 3 substrings are generic 13-16-char phrases ("who are they", "faculty of
  economics", "optimism") appearing mid-sentence in unrelated training docs —
  incidental n-gram overlap, NOT document/label contamination.

MEASURED QUALITY (boundary-F1 + literature space-correct acc)
-------------------------------------------------------------
  Metric definitions: boundary-F1 over the full candidate universe; space-
  correct accuracy over the whitespace-gap universe (the crfcut/Slayden/Zhou
  metric). All engines judged identically. crf.Default is a TAINTED baseline
  (see above), shown for comparison only.

  *** REAL hand-annotated free-prose CC0 gold (classical narrative + PD statutes,
      182 sentences) -- the most meaningful test; TEST-ONLY, disjoint ***
    engine                 bF1      spAcc
    charseg.Default        0.4501   0.6273   <- WINS boundary-F1 on real prose
    crf.Default(taint)     0.3974   0.6568
    (default has higher recall / slightly lower precision; crf edges space-acc.)

  macro over 10 datasets (equal weight per domain):
    engine                 macro-bF1   macro-spAcc
    charseg.Default          0.6632       0.6771     <- clean, releasable, BEST macro
    crf.Default(taint)       0.5585       0.6388

  micro-pooled (news-heavy, UD-dominated):
    crf.Default(taint)   bF1 0.6616  spAcc 0.7473   <- best pooled (news-weighted)
    charseg.Default      bF1 0.6182  spAcc 0.6796

  per-dataset boundary-F1 (charseg.Default vs crf.Default):
    HANDGOLD-prose 0.450  WIN (vs crf 0.397)   formal_news 0.895 WIN (vs 0.800)
    social_chat    0.800  WIN (vs 0.625)        novel_dialogue 0.755 WIN (vs 0.622)
    poetry_lyrics  0.529  WIN (crf collapses to 0.000)
    tricky_tokens  0.628  WIN (vs 0.520)  <- abbreviation/date cases
    T117-tatoeba-gold(synth) 0.910  ~tie (vs crf 0.921)
    academic_legal 0.588  (noisy 20-boundary set)
    UD_Thai-PUD    0.593  lose (vs crf 0.653)   UD_Thai-TUD 0.484 lose (vs crf 0.590)

  ฯ (paiyannoi) guard: some literary silver wrongly marked a boundary after ฯ.
  The trainer drops any boundary right after ฯ unless it is the ฯลฯ (et cetera)
  ligature (3,526 wrong boundaries dropped), fixing mid-clause honorifics like
  โปรดเกล้าฯ / กรุงเทพฯ.

HONEST SUMMARY
--------------
The clean default model WINS the macro-averaged (equal-per-domain) boundary-F1
and space-correct accuracy, fixes the crfcut poetry collapse, and is best on
dialogue / social / abbreviation-date. It does NOT beat the crfcut-derived CRF
on the two formal-news UD benchmarks or on micro-pooled (news-weighted)
accuracy: those need in-domain gold with labelled INTRA-paragraph sentence
boundaries, which no permissive Thai corpus provides. This gap is a
data-licensing limitation, reported not hidden.

